# Parsed after the AOSP service definition, whose supplementary groups are
# "camera drmrpc mediadrm" only. Two device nodes need more than that, and both
# were confirmed on the handset:
#
#   /dev/Vcodec    media:system 0660  -> needs "system"
#   /dev/MTK_SMI   media:media  0660  -> needs "media"
#
# Without "media", libbwc fails every SMI/EMI bandwidth call during encode:
#   E/BWC: Open SMI(/dev/MTK_SMI) driver file failed.:Permission denied
#   E/BWC: Failed to switch SMI profile, error: -1
#   E/BWC: fail to open mem_bw_ctrl driver file
# which is EACCES from the DAC check, not SELinux. (The node was already
# *labelled* mtk_smi_device, but nothing granted mediacodec access to that type
# -- that half was added separately in sepolicy/media/clients.te. Both halves
# were missing; only the DAC one produced the visible EACCES, because the build
# was permissive.) Stock hands this service twelve supplementary groups
# (media_rw sdcard_rw media system audio inet net_bt net_bt_admin net_bw_acct
# sdcard_r on top of AOSP's three); only the two that a shipped node actually
# requires are added here. In particular the service gets no network groups: an
# OMX component has no business holding a socket.
service vendor.media.omx /vendor/bin/hw/android.hardware.media.omx@1.0-service
    class main
    user mediacodec
    group camera drmrpc mediadrm media system
    ioprio rt 4
    writepid /dev/cpuset/foreground/tasks
    override
